WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.852 --> 00:00:08.936
Oh my God!

00:00:12.565 --> 00:00:14.066
So what are we getting?

00:00:15.109 --> 00:00:15.860
We're getting ice.

00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:20.072
We're getting...the most obvious choice.

00:00:21.490 --> 00:00:22.992
Kill the engine, brother.

00:00:24.702 --> 00:00:27.330
If you're really quiet,

00:00:27.371 --> 00:00:28.956
and you listen through the waves.

00:00:30.458 --> 00:00:31.334
You hear all the pops

00:00:31.334 --> 00:00:32.501
and cracks?

00:00:32.501 --> 00:00:32.960
Mm hmm.

00:00:33.336 --> 00:00:35.254
This is the glacier ice expansion,

00:00:35.254 --> 00:00:39.175
pressed snow and air bubbles
over thousands of years.

00:00:39.342 --> 00:00:43.387
So when it melts, all
the air bubbles pop.

00:00:43.888 --> 00:00:46.640
So if you put this in a glass
and you pour a cocktail on top of it,

00:00:47.391 --> 00:00:49.977
you're going to get the same
popping effect.

00:00:52.813 --> 00:00:55.733
I did not know glacier
ice pops and fizzes.

00:00:56.359 --> 00:00:57.443
Like, even just now.

00:00:57.443 --> 00:00:58.194
Just hold it. Just.

00:00:58.194 --> 00:01:00.696
Just take a second, everyone.

00:01:03.657 --> 00:01:06.202
Like, seriously?

00:01:07.078 --> 00:01:09.789
It's magnificent.

00:01:10.831 --> 00:01:13.876
I'm finding myself at a loss for words.

00:01:24.762 --> 00:01:26.013
[Bleep]

00:01:27.681 --> 00:01:28.933
[Bleep]

00:01:31.102 --> 00:01:35.648
No, no way.

00:01:37.691 --> 00:01:39.235
[Bleep]

00:01:40.027 --> 00:01:40.820
We're surrounded

00:01:40.820 --> 00:01:43.739
by walruses.

00:01:49.870 --> 00:01:50.538
I can stare at

00:01:50.538 --> 00:01:54.083
this all day, but let's collect
some of the glacier ice.

00:01:54.500 --> 00:01:57.086
Oh, yeah, because
we actually have stuff to do.

00:01:57.086 --> 00:01:59.964
We actually do have stuff
to do and a dinner to be prepared.

00:02:01.382 --> 00:02:02.216
Here we go.

00:02:02.425 --> 00:02:03.759
Maybe that one.

00:02:03.759 --> 00:02:05.344
Let’s see.

00:02:09.140 --> 00:02:09.682
[Bleep]

00:02:10.975 --> 00:02:14.145
Only 10% of the ice is actually above
water.

00:02:14.812 --> 00:02:17.314
It's all connected. Bye.

00:02:17.314 --> 00:02:20.818
So these pieces are a lot bigger than they
appear on the surface.

00:02:21.485 --> 00:02:22.987
Hold on. I got you.

00:02:22.987 --> 00:02:26.282
Are you sure you have me?

00:02:27.950 --> 00:02:29.243
Oh, damn.

00:02:29.243 --> 00:02:32.788
One cubic foot of ice actually weighs
55 pounds.

00:02:33.998 --> 00:02:37.334
Okay, so we're definitely going
to get our workout today.

00:02:38.169 --> 00:02:40.754
[Bleep] That's heavy.

00:02:40.838 --> 00:02:42.173
I'm going to taste it.

00:02:42.381 --> 00:02:44.133
Cheers. Cheers.

00:02:44.133 --> 00:02:46.927
Hmm. Salty.

00:02:48.262 --> 00:02:49.555
It is salty.

00:02:49.555 --> 00:02:52.391
But don't worry,
that saltiness won't be noticeable

00:02:52.391 --> 00:02:56.020
in a cocktail since the ice itself
is made from freshwater.

00:02:56.061 --> 00:03:00.399
and we'll be chipping these giant chunks
into very small pieces. Hmm.

00:03:00.608 --> 00:03:02.318
I'll bet there's walrus pee on this,
what do you say?

00:03:02.318 --> 00:03:04.570
A little bit of extra flavoring.

